# The ledger of `i18n/locales`: likely subtags and aliases from CLDR 49. One
# block per capability. The census is the one `i18n.ledger` names. Expected
# tags are what ICU 79.1 answered.

capability locale/likely  a language's likely script and region added, and taken away
  heroes  locales.add_likely_subtags, locales.remove_likely_subtags
  go      Tag.Script (with its Confidence), Tag.Region, Tag.Base
  rust    LocaleExpander::maximize, LocaleExpander::minimize (icu_locale)
  python  -
  java    -
  dotnet  -
  icu     ULocale.addLikelySubtags, ULocale.minimizeSubtags, uloc_addLikelySubtags, uloc_minimizeSubtags

capability locale/canonical  a tag canonicalized by CLDR's aliases
  heroes  locales.canonicalize
  go      language.CanonType, language.Deprecated, language.Macro, language.All
  rust    LocaleCanonicalizer::canonicalize (icu_locale)
  python  locale.normalize
  java    -
  dotnet  -
  icu     Locale.canonicalize, uloc_canonicalize
  note    language, script, region and variant aliases, a region split in many taking the language's likely one, variants sorted, `u` keywords sorted; the old values of `u` keywords (`islamicc`) are kept, where ICU replaces them

capability locale/match  the best of a program's languages for a reader, by CLDR's language matching
  heroes  pending: CLDR's distances need its match variables and paradigm locales, not carried yet; `i18n.lookup_tag` and `i18n.filter_tags` match by RFC 4647
  go      language.NewMatcher, language.Matcher.Match, language.MatchStrings, language.Comprehends, language.PreferSameScript, message.MatchLanguage
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    -
  dotnet  -
  icu     LocaleMatcher, LocaleMatcher.getBestMatch, LocaleMatcher.Builder

capability locale/validity  whether each subtag is a valid code
  heroes  pending: CLDR's validity data is not carried
  go      language.ValueError
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    -
  dotnet  -
  icu     -
